# The SLR check of a static fold (foldsim --region; foldsim_sll_check.py on the
# netlist: each copy's LUT, LUTRAM, FF, URAM and RAMB36 counted on
# foldsim_sim.mlir, an assignment of whole copies to the region's SLRs, the
# SLLs each boundary takes).
#
# --slr-policy guide (the default, 11-08 evening): a class copy crossing an SLR
# boundary is a GUIDE warning naming each straddling copy, its resources, the
# SLRs it spreads over, the projected SLLs per boundary and the suggested
# assignment of the other copies; foldsim_sim.sv is kept. Containment failed at
# every SM count and the straddled 4-SM image works on silicon (c4g, contained,
# placed no faster). The check's physical refusals still fail: the design past
# the placement fill, the memories past the region's, SLLs past a boundary
# (r16c, Place 30-5425).
#
# --slr-policy strict: the 11-08 hard rule (a copy that fits no SLR whole or is
# cut over SLRs fails, foldsim_sim.sv renamed foldsim_sim.sv.slr-refused; only
# --allow-slr-straddle=<reason> overrides it, recorded in
# <out>/SLR_STRADDLE_APPROVED and foldsim_sim.json). Under guide,
# --allow-slr-straddle is accepted and ignored (no longer needed).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/Inputs/storage

# Default: a static fold is checked against the V80 compute shell's region.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/v80 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V80
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=V80R < %t/v80/sll/sll.txt
# V80: foldsim: SLL check: v80: OK
# V80-NOT: GUIDE
# V80R: SLR2 capacity: lut 601,637
# V80R: v80: OK

# Guide: two SLRs of 110 LUTs, the Leaf copy (about 123) fits neither whole but
# the region holds the design: the copy is cut, a GUIDE warning, the netlist kept.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/split --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-split.json Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SPLIT
# RUN: test -f %t/split/foldsim_sim.sv && not test -e %t/split/foldsim_sim.sv.slr-refused
# SPLIT: foldsim: SLL check: split: OK
# SPLIT: foldsim: GUIDE: SLR straddle (a guide, --slr-policy guide)
# SPLIT-NEXT: GUIDE: Leaf straddles over SLR1 {{[0-9]+}} %/SLR0 {{[0-9]+}} %: lut {{[0-9,]+}}, lutram {{[0-9,]+}}, ff {{[0-9,]+}}, uram 0.0, bram 0.0
# SPLIT: GUIDE: suggested SLR1:
# SPLIT-NOT: error

# Guide: two Leaf copies, each fits an SLR whole but the placer fills an SLR to
# half: no assignment of whole copies, the copies cut, the SLLs projected (a
# placement model in the region): GUIDE lines with the boundary's SLLs.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cut --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:2 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-cut.json Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CUT
# RUN: test -f %t/cut/foldsim_sim.sv
# CUT: foldsim: SLL check: cut: WARN: {{.*}} cut over SLRs
# CUT: GUIDE: Leaf{{(_copy1)?}} straddles
# CUT: GUIDE: boundary SLR1-SLR0: {{[0-9,]+}} SLLs projected
# CUT-NOT: error

# Still a failure under guide: the design past the region's placement fill
# (region-fill.json: region-cut.json at a 50 % fill).
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/fill --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:2 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-fill.json Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FILL
# FILL: foldsim: SLL check: fill: REFUSE: the design's lut {{[0-9]+}} %, ff {{[0-9]+}} % of the region, past the placement fill
# FILL: foldsim: error: the SLR check refuses this netlist: REFUSE: the design's

# Guide with --allow-slr-straddle: accepted, a warning, no record.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/gall --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-split.json --allow-slr-straddle='old script' Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GALL
# RUN: not test -e %t/gall/SLR_STRADDLE_APPROVED
# GALL: foldsim: warning: --allow-slr-straddle is no longer needed

# Strict: two SLRs of 100 LUTs, the Leaf copy fits no SLR whole: the 11-08 rule.
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/tiny --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-tiny.json --slr-policy strict Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TINY
# RUN: test -f %t/tiny/foldsim_sim.sv.slr-refused && not test -e %t/tiny/foldsim_sim.sv
# TINY: foldsim: error: SLR rule: no class copy may cross an SLR boundary; this netlist: REFUSE: Leaf fits no SLR whole
# TINY-NEXT: Leaf fits no SLR whole: lut {{[0-9,]+}}, lutram {{[0-9,]+}}, ff {{[0-9,]+}}, uram 0.0, bram 0.0
# TINY-NEXT: SLR capacities (logic x margin 1.0, memories whole):
# TINY-NEXT: SLR1: lut 100, lutram 100, ff 200, uram 100.0, bram 100.0
# TINY-NEXT: SLR0: lut 100, lutram 100, ff 200, uram 100.0, bram 100.0
# TINY: foldsim_sim.sv renamed foldsim_sim.sv.slr-refused
# TINY-SAME: --allow-slr-straddle=<who, when, why>

# Strict: the cut copies, a warning of the check, a failure of the rule.
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/scut --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:2 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-cut.json --slr-policy strict Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SCUT
# SCUT: foldsim: SLL check: scut: WARN: {{.*}} cut over SLRs
# SCUT: foldsim: error: SLR rule: no class copy may cross an SLR boundary
# SCUT: Leaf{{(_copy1)?}} is left out of every assignment of whole copies to the SLRs
# SCUT: SLR1: lut 200, lutram 200, ff 400

# Strict, the override: the compilation finishes, the reason recorded.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/ovr --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 --region %S/Inputs/slr-rule/region-tiny.json --slr-policy strict --allow-slr-straddle='lit test, 11-08, synthetic' Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVR
# RUN: test -f %t/ovr/foldsim_sim.sv
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVRF < %t/ovr/SLR_STRADDLE_APPROVED
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVRJ < %t/ovr/foldsim_sim.json
# OVR: foldsim: WARNING: SLR STRADDLE APPROVED: lit test, 11-08, synthetic
# OVR-NEXT: SLR rule: no class copy may cross an SLR boundary
# OVR-NOT: --sll-check fails on it
# OVRF: "reason": "lit test, 11-08, synthetic"
# OVRF: "Leaf"
# OVRJ: "slr_straddle_approved"

# A manifest whose platform is not the V80 has no default region: no check.
# RUN: foldsim --manifest %S/Inputs/slr-rule/u55c.toml --out %t/u55c --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --copies Leaf:1 Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=U55C
# RUN: not test -e %t/u55c/sll
# U55C-NOT: SLL check
